  "conclusions": [
    "Six directional rejection publications under new H1/M5 policy: all passed recorded H1 gate, all mid-range/weak M5 timing failures; three deduplicated M5 intervals.",
    "Only one new-policy forward proxy resolved; its stop-first result is ambiguous because the candle touched both barriers. Two are not yet observable. No new-policy filter-quality conclusion is possible.",
    "Previous v2 policy: 229 timing rejection publications reduce to 74 probes, 14 positive and 60 negative under stop-first. 36 ambiguous candles prevent exact missed-winner attribution. Nonoverlap sensitivity: 67 probes, 14 positive, 53 negative; 33 ambiguous.",
    "Older-policy results do not establish performance of the new policy. No evidence here justifies blanket loosening; structural-location and momentum quality remain hypotheses for the next bounded experiment.",
